WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.610
Here's how GoCareer works, step by step.

2
00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:06.910
First for candidates, then for employers.

3
00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:12.650
A candidate starts on the welcome screen, and chooses: I'm new,

4
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:13.970
set up my profile.

5
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:19.880
Step one is the profile type: Jobs, Internship, or Consultant.

6
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:21.980
We'll follow the Jobs path.

7
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.630
Next, the candidate searches and adds target roles.

8
00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.090
In this sample, Frontend Developer.

9
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:35.110
Then an experience range, from zero to two years, up to twelve plus.

10
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:39.280
Employment type, full-time or part-time.

11
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:45.180
Then work environment: remote, hybrid, or on-site, with an option to relocate.

12
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:52.130
Finally, the account is created by verifying a phone number with a one-time

13
00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:52.510
code.

14
00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.780
Our public capture stops here.

15
00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:01.690
After sign-in, the candidate uploads a resume and taps Extract from resume.

16
00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:07.380
The profile is prefilled for review, and LinkedIn can be skipped for now.

17
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.800
From Find Jobs or AI Matches,

18
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:16.280
Recommended for you ranks open roles by how many of the candidate's skills

19
00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:16.880
overlap.

20
00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:23.580
A job page shows the role overview, skills and tags, and about the role.

21
00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:29.410
Apply now submits the profile in one click, and the button turns to Applied.

22
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:35.770
The Applications workspace tracks every role across Active, Saved, Offers,

23
00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.290
Rejected, and History.

24
00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.950
Chats start when a recruiter sends the first message.

25
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.880
Employers use the separate recruiter portal.

26
00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.740
Sign-up takes two steps: personal details, then the company,

27
00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:51.640
as a direct employer or a recruitment agency.

28
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:59.430
Post new job opens a composer that checks each required field: title,

29
00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:04.680
department, opportunity type, experience, employment type, work setup,

30
00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:09.780
location, hiring manager, target hire date, skills, and description.

31
00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:15.070
Submitted jobs are reviewed before they're published.

32
00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:19.990
Listings are organised into All, Published, Drafts, Under review,

33
00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.280
and Not approved.

34
00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:24.760
From a live listing, open the hiring pipeline.

35
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:30.890
Pipelines use editable stage templates, for example Applied, Screening,

36
00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:35.720
Shortlist, Interview, Offer, and Hired, with Rejected kept separate.

37
00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:42.250
From any candidate, a recruiter can schedule an online or physical interview,

38
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.730
reject with a reason, or create an offer letter, upload the PDF,

39
00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:49.540
and send it with Create and email offer.

40
00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:54.090
The offer arrives in the candidate's Offers tab.

41
00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:57.060
One connected process, from profile to hire.

